{"title": "The Chess Players (Eakins)", "html": "\n<div class=\"wiki-table-scroll wiki-infobox-wrap\"><table class=\"infobox vevent\"><tbody><tr><th class=\"infobox-above summary\" colspan=\"2\">The Chess Players</th></tr><tr><td class=\"infobox-image\" colspan=\"2\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\"><img class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"294\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/The_Chess_Players_MET_DT1506.jpg/500px-The_Chess_Players_MET_DT1506.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/The_Chess_Players_MET_DT1506.jpg/960px-The_Chess_Players_MET_DT1506.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"400\"></span></td></tr><tr><th class=\"infobox-label\" scope=\"row\">Artist</th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><a data-title=\"Thomas Eakins\">Thomas Eakins</a></td></tr><tr><th class=\"infobox-label\" scope=\"row\">Year</th><td class=\"infobox-data\">1876</td></tr><tr><th class=\"infobox-label\" scope=\"row\">Type</th><td class=\"infobox-data category\">Oil on wood panel</td></tr><tr><th class=\"infobox-label\" scope=\"row\">Dimensions</th><td class=\"infobox-data\">29.8&nbsp;cm \u00d7&nbsp;42.6&nbsp;cm (<span class=\"frac\">11<span class=\"sr-only\">+</span><span class=\"num\">3</span>\u2044<span class=\"den\">4</span></span>&nbsp;in \u00d7&nbsp;<span class=\"frac\">16<span class=\"sr-only\">+</span><span class=\"num\">3</span>\u2044<span class=\"den\">4</span></span>&nbsp;in)</td></tr><tr><th class=\"infobox-label\" scope=\"row\">Location</th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><div class=\"plainlist\"><ul><li><a data-title=\"Metropolitan Museum of Art\">Metropolitan Museum of Art</a>, <a data-title=\"New York City\">New York</a></li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><i><b>The Chess Players</b></i> is an 1876 <a data-title=\"Genre painting\">genre painting</a> by the American painter <a data-title=\"Thomas Eakins\">Thomas Eakins</a>, <a data-title=\"List of works by Thomas Eakins\">Goodrich catalogue #96</a>. It is in the collection of the <a data-title=\"Metropolitan Museum of Art\">Metropolitan Museum of Art</a>, in <a data-title=\"New York City\">New York</a>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"chessboard thumb noviewer floatright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\"><div class=\"wiki-table-scroll\"><table><tbody><tr><td></td><td>a</td><td>b</td><td>c</td><td>d</td><td>e</td><td>f</td><td>g</td><td>h</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td colspan=\"8\" rowspan=\"8\"><div class=\"chess-pieces notheme\"><span class=\"notpageimage\"><span><img class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"208\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Chessboard480.svg/250px-Chessboard480.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Chessboard480.svg/500px-Chessboard480.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"208\"></span></span><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"c8 black rook\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Chess_rdt45.svg/40px-Chess_rdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Chess_rdt45.svg/60px-Chess_rdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"g8 black king\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Chess_kdt45.svg/40px-Chess_kdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Chess_kdt45.svg/60px-Chess_kdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"a7 black pawn\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/40px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/60px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"e7 white bishop\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Chess_blt45.svg/40px-Chess_blt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Chess_blt45.svg/60px-Chess_blt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"f7 black pawn\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/40px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/60px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"h6 black pawn\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/40px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/60px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"e5 black bishop\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chess_bdt45.svg/40px-Chess_bdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chess_bdt45.svg/60px-Chess_bdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"g5 black pawn\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/40px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/60px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"f4 black pawn\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/40px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chess_pdt45.svg/60px-Chess_pdt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"h3 white pawn\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Chess_plt45.svg/40px-Chess_plt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Chess_plt45.svg/60px-Chess_plt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"a2 white pawn\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Chess_plt45.svg/40px-Chess_plt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Chess_plt45.svg/60px-Chess_plt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"d2 white knight\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Chess_nlt45.svg/40px-Chess_nlt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Chess_nlt45.svg/60px-Chess_nlt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"e2 black knight\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Chess_ndt45.svg/40px-Chess_ndt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Chess_ndt45.svg/60px-Chess_ndt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"h2 white king\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Chess_klt45.svg/40px-Chess_klt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Chess_klt45.svg/60px-Chess_klt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div><div><span class=\"mw-valign-top notpageimage\"><span><img alt=\"e1 white rook\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"26\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Chess_rlt45.svg/40px-Chess_rlt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Chess_rlt45.svg/60px-Chess_rlt45.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"26\"></span></span></div></div></td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>a</td><td>b</td><td>c</td><td>d</td><td>e</td><td>f</td><td>g</td><td>h</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"thumbcaption\">State of the game</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"wr-Description\">Description</h2></div>\n<p>It is a small oil on wood panel depicting Eakins' father Benjamin observing a <a data-title=\"Chess\">chess</a> match. The two players are Bertrand Gardel (at left), an elderly French teacher, and the somewhat younger George Holmes, a painter.  The men are in a dark, wood-panelled Victorian parlour with a quality of light suggesting late afternoon. The game is well in progress, as many pieces have been removed from the board. Holmes, the younger player, seems to be winning the match, as he has taken the <a data-title=\"Queen (chess)\">queen</a> of his opponent (the top of which pokes out of the table's drawer), and his own black queen is well-positioned in the centre of the board. Eakins painted <i>The Chess Players</i> for his father, and signed the painting in Latin, \"BENJAMINI. EAKINS. FILIUS. PINXIT. '76\"\u2014\"the son of Benjamin Eakins painted this\"\u2014in small letters on the drawer of the table. Michael Clapper of Franklin &amp; Marshall College has noted, \"Eakins\u2019s choice of [chess] and his knowledgeable treatment of it suggest that he was familiar with and interested in the game, though there is little direct evidence of it apart from the painting.\"\n</p><p>Art historian Akela Reason proposes that the painting is a tribute to a number of the artist's father-figures: Holmes probably was Eakins's first art teacher; Gardel was his French teacher; Benjamin Eakins was his literal father; and <a data-title=\"Jean-L\u00e9on G\u00e9r\u00f4me\">Jean-L\u00e9on G\u00e9r\u00f4me</a>, his master at the <a data-title=\"\u00c9cole des Beaux-Arts\">\u00c9cole des Beaux-Arts</a>, is represented by a print of <i>Ave Caesar Morituri te Salutant</i>, over the clock.\n</p><p>Author Martin Berger has analyzed the content of the painting in detail, finding it an evocation of the passage of time and ascribing it a highly personal meaning in Eakins' life. The younger chess player's attempt to kill the older player's <a data-title=\"King (chess)\">king</a> is analogous to the <a data-title=\"Oedipal complex\">Oedipal complex</a>. In the way that his father Benjamin is placed in opposition to Eakins the painter, the two may be envisioned as playing out a psychological \"conflict\" across the other axis of the chess board. In this light it is not coincidental that the painting was made on wood panel rather than canvas. While Eakins has humbled himself before his father in signing the painting only by reference to being Benjamin's son, he also presents his father ambivalently. Elevating his father's status, he places Benjamin centrally, with the <a data-title=\"Vanishing point\">vanishing point</a> behind Benjamin's head. Yet Eakins has obscured his father's face by shadow and by the angle at which he looks down upon the game. Although the painting was dedicated to Benjamin, the title \"The Chess Players\" curiously leaves Eakins' father out of the narrative of the picture.\n</p>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n<li class=\"gallerybox\">\n<div class=\"thumb\"><span><img alt=\"G-97. Perspective Drawing for The Chess Players (1875\u201376), Metropolitan Museum of Art.\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Perspective_drawing_for_the_Chess_players.png/120px-Perspective_drawing_for_the_Chess_players.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Perspective_drawing_for_the_Chess_players.png/250px-Perspective_drawing_for_the_Chess_players.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"95\"></span></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">G-97. Perspective Drawing for <i>The Chess Players</i> (1875\u201376), Metropolitan Museum of Art.</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\">\n<div class=\"thumb\"><span><img alt=\"G-98. Study of Bertrand Gardel for The Chess Players, Philadelphia Museum of Art.\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"120\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Bertrand_Gardel_-_Sketch_for_The_Chess_Players.png/120px-Bertrand_Gardel_-_Sketch_for_The_Chess_Players.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Bertrand_Gardel_-_Sketch_for_The_Chess_Players.png/250px-Bertrand_Gardel_-_Sketch_for_The_Chess_Players.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"99\"></span></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">G-98. Study of Bertrand Gardel for <i>The Chess Players</i>, <a data-title=\"Philadelphia Museum of Art\">Philadelphia Museum of Art</a>.</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\">\n<div class=\"thumb\"><span><img alt=\"G-188. The Writing Master: Portrait of Benjamin Eakins (1882), Metropolitan Museum of Art.\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"113\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/The_writing_master_thomas_eakins.jpeg/120px-The_writing_master_thomas_eakins.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/The_writing_master_thomas_eakins.jpeg/250px-The_writing_master_thomas_eakins.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"120\"></span></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">G-188. <i>The Writing Master: Portrait of Benjamin Eakins</i> (1882), Metropolitan Museum of Art.</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"gallerybox\">\n<div class=\"thumb\"><span><img alt=\"Engraving of The Chess Players by Eakins student Alice Barber Stephens (circa 1880).\" class=\"mw-file-element\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"97\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Chess_Players_engraving_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Chess_Players_engraving_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Chess_Players_engraving_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Chess_Players_engraving_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" width=\"120\"></span></div>\n<div class=\"gallerytext\">Engraving of <i>The Chess Players</i> by Eakins student <a data-title=\"Alice Barber Stephens\">Alice Barber Stephens</a> (circa 1880).</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "links": ["Thomas Eakins", "Metropolitan Museum of Art", "New York City", "Genre painting", "List of works by Thomas Eakins", "Chess", "Queen (chess)", "Jean-L\u00e9on G\u00e9r\u00f4me", "\u00c9cole des Beaux-Arts", "King (chess)", "Oedipal complex", "Vanishing point", "Philadelphia Museum of Art", "Alice Barber Stephens"]}